NNAAMMEE
     ffssyynncc — synchronize a file's in-core state with that on disk

SSYYNNOOPPSSIISS
     ffssyynncc _f_i_l_e _._._.

DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     The ffssyynncc utility causes all the modified data and meta-data of all the
     files named on the command line to be written to a permanent storage de‐
     vice.

     The ffssyynncc utility uses the fsync(2) function call.

EEXXIITT SSTTAATTUUSS
     If an error occurs, the ffssyynncc utility proceeds to the next file, and ex‐
     its >0.  Otherwise, it exits 0.

